  <!-- THE ORIGIN -->
  <section style="padding: var(--section-py) 0; background: var(--off-white);">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="about-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="section-eyebrow reveal">Origin</p>
          <h2 class="section-headline reveal" style="font-size:var(--text-2xl);">We started direct conversion in 1993.</h2>
          <p class="reveal" style="font-size:var(--text-base); font-weight:300; line-height:1.8; color:var(--gray-steel); margin-bottom:1rem;">
            Konstantinos Spartiotis is the founder of Simage Oy (1993), Oy Ajat Ltd. in 2001 (renamed Oy Direct Conversion Ltd. on 26.10.2019, and Oy Varex Imaging Finland Ltd. since 1.8.2023). Simage Oy was one of the earliest companies in the world to work on direct conversion X-ray imaging using CdTe. The know-how developed there was foundational. Simage Oy was granted dozens of patents in direct conversion, CdTe contact technology, and photon counting. Simage cooperated closely for years with Acrorad, Japan, to make commercial-quality CdTe. Siemens then acquired Acrorad and the Simage Oy patent portfolio.
          </p>
          <p class="reveal" style="font-size:var(--text-base); font-weight:300; line-height:1.8; color:var(--gray-steel); margin-bottom:1rem;">
            Ajat Oy became the global standard in direct conversion CdTe-CMOS dental panoramic and cephalometric imaging. Under his leadership, Ajat reached €12M in annual revenue, was highly profitable, and deployed thousands of units worldwide. Ajat Oy was sold to XCounter AB in 2009, and the group was later sold to Varex Imaging Inc. in 2019.
          </p>
          <p class="reveal" style="font-size:var(--text-base); font-weight:300; line-height:1.8; color:var(--gray-steel);">
            Athlos was founded to continue that tradition — with the same core team and new members to ensure continuity, the same technical depth and passion, and a new generation of direct conversion products: DC-Air&reg;, Ultra-Fast Scanning Sensor, and Industrial IP67 TDI, all manufactured in-house and at the VTT Micronova facility. Designed in Finland. Made in Finland.
          </p>

          <aside id="konstantinos-spartiotis" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/Person" style="display:flex;align-items:flex-start;gap:1rem;padding:1.25rem 1.5rem;margin:2rem 0 0;border-left:3px solid #43A1D8;background:#F4F7F8;border-radius:0 8px 8px 0;">
